{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/986933-kindred-of-the-east-out-of-curiosity","id":986933,"title":"Kindred of the East, Out of Curiosity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-13T13:49:09-07:00","id":986933,"title":"Kindred of the East, Out of Curiosity","content":"Will they be creating a 20 KoE? If so I'd be interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10501-laura","name":"Laura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10501_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T23:07:41-07:00","id":987114,"title":"","content":"It was published in 1998, and I suposse it should be compatible with the Vampire: the Masquerade 5th Ed (20a is the 4th).<br /> <br /> My opinion is: maybe, why not? I hope dhampires in the corebook, and the sih, the oriental &quot;cazavampires&quot; in a sourcebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T08:53:26-07:00","id":987276,"title":"","content":"I heard someone in OP claimed they hated the series, so...<br /> <br /> Anyway, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said something interesting about the matter<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/914238-are-the-kuei-jin-still-canon?p=914269#post914269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with some of the Onyx Path team and doing KotE20 is a mixture of a lot of factors. The basic dilemma is that KotE has a lot of really problematic elements in it that are in many ways hard coded into the systems (so not just fluff retcons). If KotE20 is done as a proper collection of the original, it has to include the bias inherent in the system. If KotE20 is redone to the extent needed to address its problematic elements, it loses too much of what makes KotE what it is to its fans.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of disagreement with that position, but that's what's been expressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:52:35-07:00","id":987421,"title":"","content":"Beyond not really buying the idea that changing KotE materials in order to excise the problematic elements(which was already happening with later materials when it was being published), I am glad that White Wolf is looking to continue all the lines including KotE so more than likely going to wait for that material rather than 20th. Especially since they look to actually get writers from the regions for the material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:52:55-07:00","id":987456,"title":"","content":"I've never heard of any of the current OP staff or regular freelancers actually hate KotE (and some are openly fans), some are, as I referenced though, not enthused with KotE20th as a thing (also keeping in mind the comments were made well before the Paradox purchase of the WW IPs and a the possibility of a much more heavily revised KotE in the One WoD).<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that one of the more prominent people that I was referencing in that post actually lives in Japan, and has put effort into at least getting the feel of the Japanese RPG scene's feeling on the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T03:26:28-07:00","id":987693,"title":"","content":"5e or 20th ann, I am fine with either....as long they do not make Wan Kuei Kindred that speak Cantonese....like one freelance writer wanted to do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T08:26:03-07:00","id":987762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/986933-kindred-of-the-east-out-of-curiosity?p=987693#post987693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5e or 20th ann, I am fine with either....as long they do not make Wan Kuei Kindred that speak Cantonese....like one freelance writer wanted to do</div> </div> </div> </div>Particularly given how Wan Gui is the Mandarin reading.<br /> <br /> [/missing the point]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T01:37:08-07:00","id":988184,"title":"","content":"So long as they don't all originate from a mythological Middle Eastern murderer (not even in a nudge, nudge, wink, wink way like KotEK), I'll be happy. It was popular for combining elements of Wraith (Psyche/Shadow), Werewolf (Stepping Sideways, caerns, fetishes), Mage (seekings and Arete) and Vampire (blood drinking, Disciplines), and I think those parts are the bits people would object to losing. The racist stuff can be excised while keeping those other bits and the focus can be broadened from just China with the terminology (or regional variations can be given).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T20:03:06-07:00","id":989167,"title":"","content":"This is great, I will be watching this if they do start up the idea.. as they done with others. I'd like to add it to my chronicles which Im having all of 20th Anniversary setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10501-laura","name":"Laura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10501_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}